Except for footprints left by rough shoes, Ragnar noticed monster tracks: half as large as his own feet, with four fingers clasped tight to one another. They were covering the ground in a two meters radius, but led nowhere. Another pair of tracks, unusual for this place, caught his eye: rather small, neat, well sized and expensive shoes which were so unlike the wooden shoes of the water carriers. It was also curious that footprints of those feet could be seen on the road to the well and by the shrubs nearby. Ragnar hemmed thoughtfully and went to the caves.